    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0301" n="225" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg225"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1818</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Russell </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-05-07T12:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 7, 1916, noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your May 6, 6 a.m., received May 7, 10 a.m. Caperton reports to Navy Department
                    May 6, midnight, that President has canceled request that city be occupied by
                    our forces and has placed his resignation in your hands May 6, 9 p.m.</p>
                <p>While naturally desirous that bloodshed be avoided, Department believes that
                    manifestly irregular manner of impeachment renders it particularly desirable
                    that President be upheld by every possible and proper means. Previous
                    instructions to you and to naval forces grant authority for such action as you
                    may deem advisable.</p>
                <p>Additional marines are being sent and Caperton so advised.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
